  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "9eXWGZSkUsIquYDE9C+w9NV+Qkw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:53.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Integrated Project Delivery (IPD) projects involve multiple disciplines working together from the beginning \u2014 clients, construction masters, consultants (DT BAU, 01:15:53).\n\nThe governing documents (BEP) are **discussed and agreed collectively** in IPD, contrasting with traditional projects that suffer from conflicts (01:27:36). What makes that collaboration real rather than aspirational is the incentive structure: **cost savings are shared among participating companies**, encouraging genuine team collaboration and collective document management (01:28:55).\n\nTwo implications for a document-model platform:\n- Multi-party documents with attributable history map directly onto IPD's collective authorship needs \u2014 every stakeholder edit is visible and accountable.\n- Incentive-aligned projects are the most receptive early market for shared, live documents; adversarial traditional contracts are the least.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T18:11:53.396384+00:00"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:53.000Z"
    }
  },
